From d5cc46cf18bc7e4839e80380335ce582386e7988 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jingledingle521 <36874370+jingledingle521@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 08:03:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] App Store: Updates and Settings pages, sidebar follows
 links, icons
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Updates: a large title, "Available" with the count and size, an accent
  Update All pill; plainer rows; the footer only while installing.
- Settings: a large title; each source's rows in a rounded panel with a
  switch and a ⋯ menu (priority, remove, contents).
- The sidebar's selection follows the page at the bottom of the stack, so
  categories, searches and apps opened from links or the command line
  select the right section (or none).
- App icons come from the icon theme by AppStream id when it has them
  (WhiteSur restyles them; Fedora's Flatpak catalog leaves some without
  one). PackageKit: find cached icons AppStream hands back as bare file
  names; Flatpak: OCI remotes keep icons without an "active" checkout.
- The search field just says Search; MAC_TEST_TOUR=<dir> saves pictures
  of the main pages (MacTour).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KdkdNUmoM62iDwjRop6X5f
